## ctx.windowId implementation (the key unlock, P19j)

Per-window panel ownership / primary-active needs the server to know which window a
WS connection belongs to. Three pieces:

1. `packages/shared/transport/src/server/context.ts` — added optional field to `TrpcContext`:
   `windowId?: number | null` (nullable — null on standalone CLI/agent connections).
2. `packages/shared/transport/src/server/ws-server.ts` — `createContext({ req })` now parses
   `?windowId=N` from `req.url` (try/catch around `new URL(...)`, coerce via `Number.isFinite`,
   else `null`), returns `{ ...baseContext, req, windowId }`.
3. Per-procedure handling in `routers/app.ts`:
   - `taskWindows.setPrimaryActive` → passes `ctx.windowId ?? null` (primary-only check inside op).
   - `taskWindows.claimPanel / releasePanel / releaseAllForTask / claimAndCloseOther / claimSession`
     and `window.close` → `if (ctx.windowId == null) throw new Error('windowId required')`.
   - `taskWindows.getWindowId` → returns null when `ctx.windowId == null` (null-safe).
   - `taskWindows.onPanelCloseRequest` (sub) → filters `if (ctx.windowId !== targetWindowId) return`
     so the close-request is delivered only to the matching window's connection.

windowId === webContents.id (same value IPC uses via `event.sender.id`), so IPC and tRPC stay
consistent when the renderer migrates in slice 5. **Backward-compat:** current renderer connects
WITHOUT `?windowId` → `ctx.windowId === null`; the windowId-requiring procedures throw, but no
tRPC client calls them yet (renderer still on IPC). Inert for every existing router.

## Sustainability (one impl, two adapters)

Every commit: IPC handler + tRPC procedure both delegate to ONE shared thing — no duplicated
behavior. Shared ops extracted where the IPC handler held inline logic:
- `browserExtensionOps` (index.ts) — 6 chrome-extension ops.
- `webviewOps` (index.ts, module scope) — devtools + shortcuts + emulation; lifted
  `registeredWebviews`/`keyboardPassthroughWebviews`/`webviewEvents` to module scope.
- `taskWindowsOps` + `taskWindowsEvents` (task-windows.ts); `primaryActiveTaskId` lifted to module scope.
- `floatingGlobalAgentPanelOps` + `floatingGlobalAgentPanelEvents` (floating-global-agent-panel.ts).
- `browserViewEvents` (browser-view-manager.ts).
- Browser view ops delegate to the existing `browserViewManager` singleton; dialog to electron `dialog`.

**Dual-emit:** every subscription source keeps its existing `webContents.send(...)` AND adds
`emitter.emit(...)`, tagged `// legacy IPC (slice 5 drops)` so slice 5 can grep-and-kill. The tRPC
emitters fan out to zero subscribers until slice 5 — pure no-op now, cannot break the live IPC renderer.

